  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nLittle change is expected to the upper-level pattern and our local \nweather through the extended forecast period when compared to the \nshort term forecast period. The ridge will gradually amplify toward \nthe end of the workweek, with guidance converging on a common \nplacement of the ridge axis just east of the Great Plains. This will \nkeep the thermal ridge mostly in place over the Middle Mississippi \nValley and 850 mb temperatures steady. Toward the end of the \nweekend, some guidance shows that a backdoor front may push the \nthermal ridge westward and take the edge off of the heat, but a \nmajority of guidance currently shows it continuing. \n\nAn uninterrupted fetch of Gulf moisture into the area supports dew \npoints increasing through the end of the week, though by high much \nremains uncertain. Guidance consensus is that the CWA will be on the \nnorthern periphery of greater dew points through the period, with \nslight changes in the placement of the upper-level ridge dictating \nthe exact placement of this moisture. Confidence is high that \nsurface winds will be southwesterly daily, leading to a local \ndecrease in dew points thanks to downsloping off the Ozarks. These \nfactors combined with a seasonal dearth in evapotranspiration lead \nto low confidence in the NBM's dew points. Current values lead to \npockets of heat index values just over 105 degrees, and if that is \nrealized, a targeted Extreme Heat Warning may be needed. If dew \npoints trend lower than currently forecast, the Heat Advisory will \ncontinue through the end of the week area-wide.",
